# Drive the DN3500 boot PROM from power-on to Domain/OS, for
# `apollo-headless --boot-script`.
#
#   apollo-headless --boot-prom roms/firmware/3500_BOOT_12191_7.bin \
#       --disk media/dn3500-sr10.4-installed.awd --boot-console \
#       --boot-input $'\r' --boot-input-port 1 --boot-input-channel B \
#       --boot-script tools/boot-domainos.script
#
# The carriage return in `--boot-input` is not part of the dialogue: the PROM
# autobauds, so it cannot transmit until it has received a character, and a
# console nobody types at never says anything at all.
#
# The one question the PROM asks is the loaded SELF_TEST diagnostic's, after it
# reports that the configuration table in the calendar's battery-backed RAM is
# uninitialised. Answering **y** continues past that -- it is a setup step and
# not a fault -- and every test then passes.
#
# **That question is conditional, and a script must not be written as though it
# were not.** SELF_TEST asks it when the configuration table disagrees with the
# machine; a node whose table describes it correctly prints `Self tests passed.`
# and asks nothing. `--ring-two-node` builds such a node, and its dialogue --
# copied from this one -- waited for ever on a prompt that never came, typing
# nothing for forty-two minutes (`FINDINGS.md` C193). This file stays as it is
# because the single-machine path really does boot with an uninitialised
# configuration; anything else should expect a line the boot always prints.
expect Do you wish to continue
send y\r
